+# Porting notes: Trojita v0.7 → Qt 4.8 (macOS PowerPC / MacPorts)
+
+This branch (`qt4-0.7`, based on tag `v0.7`) restores Qt4 buildability that was
+removed from upstream right after v0.6, so that the macos-powerpc `trojita`
+Portfile can move from v0.6 to v0.7. Full task spec: `QT4-BACKPORT-TASK.md`.
+
+## ⚠️ Top residual risk: zero local build/test verification
+
+**No compile, no test run, no runtime check has been performed for this patch
+series.** The dev VM used to write these patches has 1 CPU / ~1GB RAM (with
+swap already in use) and no usable docker socket for the intended Ubuntu
+18.04 Qt4+Qt5 validation container (Phase 0/5 of the task spec). By explicit
+decision, the entire series was produced by manual review, mining the v0.6
+tree for the pre-removal Qt4 idioms, and grep-based completeness audits
+against the checklist in `QT4-BACKPORT-TASK.md` — with **no compilation at
+any point**.
+
+Concretely, none of the following has been checked:
+- Does `cmake -DWITH_QT5=OFF ..` actually configure?
+- Does the Qt4 build actually compile (all of `src/`, `tests/`)?
+- Does the Qt5 build still compile after the connect-syntax conversion?
+- Does either test suite run, let alone pass?
+- Does the binary start under Qt4 without `QObject::connect: No such
+  signal/slot` warnings?
+- Do the static and shared plugin configurations actually register plugins?
+
+**Whoever builds this next (real Mac, or the Ubuntu 18.04 container described
+in `QT4-BACKPORT-TASK.md` Phase 0) should treat first-build failures as
+expected, not as evidence the approach was wrong**, and should run the
+Phase 5 configuration matrix and the mechanical connect audit (Phase 3,
+verification bullet 3) before trusting this branch.
+
+## What was done
+
+1. **Build system** (`2a67666a`) — restored dual Qt4/Qt5 CMake: `WITH_QT5`
+   option (default ON), Qt4 module detection (`QtCore QtGui QtNetwork QtSql
+   QtWebKit QtSvg`, `QtDBus`/`QtTest` conditionally), external `QtMimeTypes`
+   (`devel/qt4-mimetypes`) wired via `pkg_check_modules` with a
+   `find_path`/`find_library` fallback, `WITH_CRYPTO_MESSAGES` made to depend
+   on `WITH_QT5` (GpgME++'s Qt integration is Qt5-only), translations
+   (`Qt5LinguistForTrojita`) guarded to the Qt5 branch only.
+2. **Ifdef restoration** (`436551e4`) — `git revert -n af84b80c` +
+   `git revert -n e76c8774`, resolved against v0.7's current code (~20 files
+   had real conflicts from v0.7 refactors: async `PasswordDialog`, the
+   `QLineEdit::addAction`/`setClearButtonEnabled` clear-button rework, etc.).
+   This also happened to restore the plugin dual-export machinery
+   (`Q_PLUGIN_METADATA` under a Qt5 guard, `Q_EXPORT_PLUGIN2` under a Qt4
+   guard) for all three plugins, since those files were part of the revert.
+3. **Post-v0.6 API compatibility** (`860563cd`) — the Qt5-only API surface
+   that entered the tree in the 241 commits between v0.6 and v0.7 and that
+   the af84b80c revert couldn't cover: a `QStringLiteral` shim
+   (`src/Common/Qt4Compat.h`), `QUrlQuery`/`QStandardPaths`/`toHtmlEscaped`/
+   `setSectionResizeMode` per-site `#if QT_VERSION` guards, and the
+   `QGuiApplication::applicationStateChanged` connect guarded out entirely
+   for Qt4 (no equivalent; power-saving nicety only).
+4. **Signal/slot conversion** (`7f7c41cf`, `fc5aefa6`, `1affa127`,
+   `751d7722`) — converted all new-style `connect()`/`disconnect()` calls
+   (626 connects + 21 disconnects in `src/`, 11 more in `tests/`, across 77
+   files) to the string-based `SIGNAL()`/`SLOT()` form Qt4 understands, split
+   into four commits by area (Imap+tests, Gui, Composer/Cryptography/MSA/
+   Streams/UiUtils, Plugins). Every signature was looked up against its
+   declaring class; ~18 lambda connects were refactored into named private
+   slots plus member state where the lambda captured locals.
+5. **Plugins** — see point 2; no separate commit was needed beyond the
+   connect-syntax fixes folded into the Plugins commit above, since the
+   export/static-import machinery came back with the ifdef revert.
+
+## Completeness checklist (grep-based, per `QT4-BACKPORT-TASK.md`)
+
+Run against the finished branch (not against actual Qt4/Qt5 compilation —
+see the risk section above):
+
+| Check | Original count | Now | Notes |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| new-style `connect()` | 626 (+11 tests) | 2 | Both inside `#if QT_VERSION >= QT_VERSION_CHECK(5,...)` guards: `Window.cpp`'s `applicationStateChanged` (no Qt4 equivalent) and `MessageListWidget.cpp`'s `QAction::triggered` lambda under the Qt-5.2-only `addAction(LeadingPosition)` path (has a full Qt4 fallback below it) |
+| new-style `disconnect()` | 21 | 0 | |
+| lambda connects | ~18 | 1 | Same `MessageListWidget.cpp` exception above |
+| `Q_PLUGIN_METADATA` | — | 3/3 guarded | AbookAddressbook, ClearTextPassword, QtKeyChainPassword all have matching `Q_EXPORT_PLUGIN2` under the Qt4 branch |
+| `toHtmlEscaped`/`setSectionResizeMode`/`QUrlQuery`/`QStandardPaths`/`QGuiApplication` | — | present but all `#if`-guarded or behind the `QStringLiteral`-style shim | expected; the checklist's intent is "guarded or shimmed", not "zero occurrences" |
+
+A separate mechanical audit — extracting every `SIGNAL()`/`SLOT()` pair and
+verifying it against the sender/receiver class declaration (chasing base
+classes) — was run as part of preparing this branch; see the branch's commit
+history / conversation record for details if a discrepancy surfaces during
+the real build. **This audit is static analysis, not a substitute for
+`QT_FATAL_WARNINGS=1` at runtime** — a typo'd signal/slot name is invisible
+until something actually tries to fire that connection.
+
+## Residual risks, beyond "nothing has compiled yet"
+
+- **No test exercises most GUI-side connects.** Trojita's test suite
+  (`tests/`) is concentrated on `Imap`/protocol logic and a handful of
+  formatting tests; the ~600 GUI connects converted in the Gui/Composer
+  commits (menus, dialogs, the message view, the composer) have no automated
+  coverage. A silently-broken `SIGNAL`/`SLOT` string in, say,
+  `SettingsDialog.cpp` or `ComposeWidget.cpp` would only surface by manually
+  clicking through the app under `QT_FATAL_WARNINGS=1`.
+- **The lambda-to-slot refactors are the highest-risk hand-edits** in this
+  series — they're the only Phase 3 work that isn't a mechanical string
+  substitution. Worth a manual second look: `CompleteMessageWidget.cpp`,
+  `MailBoxTreeView.cpp` (2 sites), `MessageHeadersWidget.cpp`,
+  `MessageListWidget.cpp`, `MessageSourceWidget.cpp`, `MessageView.cpp`,
+  `SimplePartWidget.cpp`, `Window.cpp` (3 sites, one of which — the
+  `QTimer::singleShot` lambda — is dual-Qt with no guard).
+- **QtWebKit API drift** between v0.6 and v0.7 in `EmbeddedWebView.cpp` /
+  `SimplePartWidget.cpp` was reviewed by reading the diff, not by compiling
+  against Qt4's QtWebKit 2.2 — the container's bionic QtWebKit is the
+  intended oracle for this and hasn't run yet.
+- **Container vs. target platform gap**: even once the Ubuntu 18.04
+  container build is green, it validates X11 Qt4, not Cocoa qt4-mac, and
+  x86_64, not big-endian PowerPC. No byte-order assumptions were
+  knowingly introduced, but this wasn't verified by a big-endian build.
+- **`libQtMimeTypes` runtime data**: it reads the freedesktop shared MIME
+  database via XDG data paths. If MIME lookups return only
+  `application/octet-stream` (in the container or on the target), the port
+  additionally needs a `shared-mime-info` dependency and/or an
+  `XDG_DATA_DIRS` hint pointing at `${prefix}/share`. Not yet checked either
+  way.
+
+## Recommended Portfile changes
+
+```
+version             0.7
+# ... existing patchfiles replaced by/augmented with format-patch output
+#     from patches/, generated via `git format-patch v0.7..qt4-0.7`
+depends_lib-append  port:qt4-mimetypes
+
+configure.args-append \
+    -DWITH_QT5=OFF \
+    -DWITH_SHARED_PLUGINS=OFF \
+    -DWITH_CRYPTO_MESSAGES=OFF \
+    -DWITH_DBUS=OFF \
+    -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PLUGIN_DIR=${prefix}/lib/trojita
+```
+
+Notes on these flags:
+- `WITH_SHARED_PLUGINS=OFF` (static plugins) is deliberate, not just a
+  container-validation convenience: Qt4/macOS `QPluginLoader` is fragile —
+  this is what silently broke the v0.6 port (every diagnostic in
+  `PluginManager.cpp` is behind `#ifdef PLUGIN_DEBUG`, so the original
+  failure mode was "cannot find storage backend" with no further detail).
+- `WITH_CRYPTO_MESSAGES=OFF` is required, not optional, for the Qt4 build —
+  the cmake option now depends on `WITH_QT5`.
+- `WITH_QTKEYCHAIN_PLUGIN` is left at its default (`AUTO`) above; turn it ON
+  explicitly if/when the target ports tree's qt4 qtkeychain is confirmed
+  present and working — the Qt4 code path for this plugin was kept intact.
+- The Ubuntu container validation additionally used
+  `-DWITH_QTKEYCHAIN_PLUGIN=OFF` only because bionic has no qt4 qtkeychain
+  package; that's a container artifact, not a recommendation for the
+  Portfile.
+
+## Next steps for whoever builds this
+
+1. Configure and build with `-DWITH_QT5=OFF` first; iterate on compile
+   errors (expected — see risk section).
+2. Once it compiles, run the test suite and grep the output for
+   `QObject::connect: No such signal/slot` with `QT_FATAL_WARNINGS=1` set.
+3. Manually exercise the GUI paths listed under "residual risks" above,
+   especially the lambda-refactored ones.
+4. Re-run the Phase 5 configuration matrix from `QT4-BACKPORT-TASK.md`
+   (Qt5 baseline, Qt4 static plugins, Qt4 shared plugins).
+5. Report back anything broken — this branch was produced without a single
+   compile, so first-pass build errors are the expected next step, not a
+   sign the patches are wrong.
