+# Task: Backport Trojita v0.7 to Qt 4.8 for macOS (PowerPC / MacPorts)
+
+## Mission
+
+Produce a patch series on top of the `v0.7` tag of this repository (the Trojita IMAP
+client) that makes it build and run correctly against **Qt 4.8.7**, for consumption by
+a MacPorts Portfile targeting **PowerPC macOS (10.4–10.6)**. The current port ships
+v0.6, which is the last upstream release with Qt4 support; Qt4 was deliberately removed
+right after v0.6 in six commits, and v0.7 then accumulated Qt5-only API during the 241
+commits between the tags. Your job is to undo that, guided by the v0.6 tree, which
+contains a working dual-Qt4/Qt5 version of almost every construct you need.
+
+Work happens entirely in this repo (`/home/sgr/barracuda/trojita`). Create a branch
+`qt4-0.7` based on the tag `v0.7` and commit all work there. Never commit to `master`.
+
+## Target platform — read this first, it decides what matters
+
+- **OS:** macOS 10.4–10.6 on PowerPC. **Big-endian.** Do not introduce any byte-order
+  assumptions (no raw casts of multi-byte integers to byte buffers, etc.).
+- **Toolchain:** FSF GCC from MacPorts (modern GCC, C++11 fully available), **not**
+  Apple clang. C++11 is fine and required (the code uses `std::async`); C++14+ is not
+  guaranteed — do not introduce anything beyond C++11.
+- **Qt:** qt4-mac 4.8.7 with QtCore, QtGui, QtNetwork, QtSql, QtWebKit, QtSvg, QtTest.
+  No QtDBus on macOS (assume `WITH_DBUS=OFF`). Qt4 has **no** QtWidgets module — all
+  widget classes live in QtGui.
+- **ObjC++:** the v0.7 tree has been audited and contains **zero** Objective-C/ObjC++
+  files and zero macOS-specific sources — do not take this task as a reason to add any.
+  If, against expectation, you must write platform glue in ObjC++, it must compile with
+  **GCC's Objective-C++ frontend**, not clang: classic `[receiver message]` syntax only,
+  no blocks (`^{...}` is a clang extension), no ARC, no dot-property syntax, no
+  `@autoreleasepool` (use `NSAutoreleasePool` explicitly), no clang-only attributes.
+- Anything not built on macOS is **out of scope**: the Harmattan/QML mobile UI, the
+  XtConnect server component (`WITH_XTCONNECT`, off by default), KDE/Akonadi plugins,
+  NSIS/Windows packaging, Linux .desktop/appdata install rules (leave them in place,
+  just don't spend effort on them), and translations (see Phase 1).
+
+## Ground rules
+
+1. **Keep the tree dual-buildable (Qt4 and Qt5) wherever it costs nothing.** This is
+   cheaper than it sounds: old-style `SIGNAL()/SLOT()` connects compile and work on
+   Qt5 too, named slots replacing lambdas work on both, and the v0.6 idiom for
+   everything else is `#if QT_VERSION >= QT_VERSION_CHECK(5, 0, 0)` guards. Dual
+   buildability is also your main verification tool (see Phase 0). If some spot is
+   genuinely painful to keep dual, prioritize Qt4 correctness — the only real consumer
+   of this patch series is the Qt4 port.
+2. **Mine v0.6 instead of inventing.** For nearly every problem you hit, the solved
+   version exists: `git show v0.6:<path>` or `git diff v0.7 v0.6 -- <path>`. Match its
+   style (guard macros, naming) exactly.
+3. The six commits that removed Qt4, in order of usefulness to you:
+   - `af84b80c` "Remove (most of) Qt4-specific #ifdefs" — 86 files, ~726 deleted lines
+     of exactly the guards you need back. Its **revert** is your Phase 2 starting point.
+   - `30094392` "cmake: remove support for Qt4" — deleted the Qt4 build-system branches
+     **and** the bundled `src/mimetypes-qt4/` QMimeDatabase backport (~37k lines).
+   - `5eb88fad` "Remove Qt4 plugins" — includes the `Q_EXPORT_PLUGIN2` dual-export
+     pattern (also removed KDE plugins; do NOT restore those).
+   - `e76c8774` "Remove wrapper around QAIM::{begin,end}ResetModel" — small.
+   - `57a8b275` "cmake: remove obsolete Qt4 support for linguist" — skip (translations
+     are out of scope).
+   - `25fa59a3` "cmake: killing some Qt4 stuff harder" — small cmake macro bits.
+4. Reverts will conflict (241 commits of drift). Use `git revert -n <sha>`, resolve
+   conflicts by consulting the v0.6 version of the file, and fold the result into your
+   own logically-organized commits. Do not leave half-applied revert commits.
+5. No behavior changes beyond Qt4 compatibility. No whitespace churn. No drive-by
+   refactoring.
+6. Commit in logical units (suggested series at the end). Each commit message should
+   say what class of incompatibility it addresses.
+
+## Phase 0 — validation environment (do this before touching code)
+
+The dev machine is Ubuntu 24.04 x86_64 with docker available. Neither Qt4 nor
+Qt5WebKit exists in 24.04, so build in an `ubuntu:18.04` container — bionic has BOTH
+Qt 4.8.7 (same version as qt4-mac!) and Qt 5.9 with QtWebKit, letting you verify both
+configurations of the dual build:
+
+```sh
+docker run -d --name trojita-qt4 -v /home/sgr/barracuda/trojita:/src ubuntu:18.04 sleep infinity
+docker exec trojita-qt4 bash -c '
+  sed -i -e "s|archive.ubuntu.com|old-releases.ubuntu.com|g" \
+         -e "s|security.ubuntu.com|old-releases.ubuntu.com|g" /etc/apt/sources.list
+  apt-get update && DEBIAN_FRONTEND=noninteractive apt-get install -y \
+    build-essential cmake pkg-config zlib1g-dev \
+    libqt4-dev libqt4-sql-sqlite libqtwebkit-dev \
+    qtbase5-dev libqt5webkit5-dev libqt5svg5-dev libqt5sql5-sqlite qttools5-dev'
+```
+
+(If old-releases has moved, any mirror carrying bionic works; the point is: gcc ≥ 5,
+cmake ≥ 3.x, Qt 4.8.7, Qt 5.9 + WebKit in one image.)
+
+No distro packages the Qt4 QMimeDatabase backport, so build it in the container the
+same way the target port does (add `git` to the apt install list):
+
+```sh
+docker exec trojita-qt4 bash -c '
+  git clone https://github.com/d1vanov/qt4-mimetypes /opt/qt4-mimetypes &&
+  cd /opt/qt4-mimetypes && git checkout f7a4aba73d378f9979974403fc3dad9a5d1f3ddc &&
+  qmake-qt4 && make -j$(nproc)'
+```
+
+Then install the headers to `/usr/local/include/QtMimeTypes/` and the built library
+to `/usr/local/lib/` (inspect the .pro for install targets; copying by hand is fine —
+this only needs to mirror the Mac port's layout: forwarding headers `QMimeDatabase`,
+`QMimeType` plus `qmime*.h` in one dir, `libQtMimeTypes.so`). Run `ldconfig`
+afterwards. If no `QtMimeTypes.pc` gets generated, write a minimal one or rely on the
+find_path/find_library fallback you add in Phase 1 — the Mac port does ship the .pc.
+
+**Baseline first:** build pristine `v0.7` with Qt5 in the container and run the test
+suite (`ctest`). Record which tests pass — that's your reference. Some may fail for
+environmental reasons; what matters is that the set of passing tests does not shrink
+after your changes.
+
+Build out-of-source, e.g. `/src/_build-qt5` and `/src/_build-qt4` (add both to
+`.git/info/exclude`, don't commit them).
+
+## Phase 1 — build system
+
+Restore the dual-Qt CMake system, using `git show v0.6:CMakeLists.txt` as the template
+and the reverts of `30094392` + `25fa59a3` as raw material. Concretely:
+
+- Reintroduce the `WITH_QT5` option (default ON to keep upstream behavior; the
+  Portfile will pass `-DWITH_QT5=OFF`).
+- Qt4 branch: `find_package(Qt4 4.8)`, modules QtCore QtGui QtNetwork QtSql QtWebKit
+  QtSvg (+ QtTest when `WITH_TESTS`, QtDBus only when `WITH_DBUS`). v0.6 used
+  `qt4_wrap_cpp` / `qt4_wrap_ui` / `qt4_add_resources` and a
+  `trojita_check_qt4_module` helper — copy that structure. Note v0.7's CMakeLists was
+  restructured relative to v0.6 (per-target `qt5_use_modules`, new source groups like
+  `src/Cryptography/`), so this is a merge, not a copy: keep v0.7's target/source
+  layout, add the Qt4 halves.
+- QMimeDatabase on Qt4: do **not** restore the vendored `src/mimetypes-qt4/` bundle
+  that v0.6 carried and `30094392` deleted. The same backport exists as a standalone
+  library, packaged in the target ports tree as `devel/qt4-mimetypes` (upstream
+  `d1vanov/qt4-mimetypes`, commit `f7a4aba`, built with qmake). Its install layout on
+  the target:
+  headers `${prefix}/include/QtMimeTypes/` (incl. `QMimeDatabase` and `QMimeType`
+  forwarding headers), library `libQtMimeTypes.dylib`, pkg-config `QtMimeTypes.pc`.
+  In the Qt4 CMake branch, detect it via `pkg_check_modules(QTMIMETYPES REQUIRED
+  QtMimeTypes)` with a `find_path`/`find_library` fallback (`qmimedatabase.h` under
+  `PATH_SUFFIXES QtMimeTypes`, library `QtMimeTypes`), add its include dir to the
+  global Qt4 include path, and link it into the targets that use it. Because the
+  include dir points *inside* `QtMimeTypes/`, the existing
+  `#include <QMimeDatabase>` lines in the four user files compile **unchanged** —
+  the only acceptable outcome; if the backport's API is missing something the four
+  call sites use, patch the call site under a Qt4 guard, don't vendor.
+- Crypto (`WITH_CRYPTO_MESSAGES`, needs Mimetic + GpgME++): make the option depend on
+  `WITH_QT5` in cmake (GpgME++'s Qt integration is Qt5-tied). The Qt4 build compiles
+  without `src/Cryptography/` GpgME parts; check how the source lists are gated and
+  keep the delegate/model fallback path (`WITH_CRYPTO_MESSAGES=OFF` already builds on
+  v0.7 Qt5 — verify that, then make Qt4 imply it).
+- QtKeychain plugin: optional. Bionic has no qt4 qtkeychain — build the Qt4 config
+  with `-DWITH_QTKEYCHAIN_PLUGIN=OFF` in the container. Keep the plugin's Qt4 code
+  path intact (v0.6 supported it; the PPC port does have a qt4 qtkeychain).
+- Translations: skip for Qt4 (do not restore `FindLinguistForTrojita.cmake` for Qt4;
+  guard the l10n rules under `WITH_QT5`).
+- `Qt5Svg` is `REQUIRED` in v0.7 — the code only loads `.svg` icons from resources at
+  runtime; for Qt4 add QtSvg to the module list so the svg image/icon plugins ship.
+
+Milestone: `cmake -DWITH_QT5=OFF ..` configures successfully (compilation will still
+fail — that's Phases 2–3).
+
+## Phase 2 — mechanical API compatibility
+
+Start from `git revert -n af84b80c` (restores most `#if QT_VERSION` guards) and
+`git revert -n e76c8774` (restores the `RESET_MODEL`-style wrapper — check what v0.6
+called it). Then fix the constructs that entered the tree *after* the removal, which
+the reverts cannot cover. Audited inventory of v0.7 `src/` (verify each with grep;
+counts are exact as of the audit):
+
+| Construct | Count / files | Fix |
+|---|---|---|
+| `QStringLiteral` | 835 uses | Central shim, one place included everywhere (v0.6 had none, so pick a home — `src/Common/` or `configure.cmake.h`): `#if QT_VERSION < QT_VERSION_CHECK(5,0,0)` → `#define QStringLiteral(str) QString::fromUtf8(str)`. Do NOT touch 835 call sites. |
+| `.toHtmlEscaped()` | 21 uses | v0.6 pattern is per-site `#if` with `Qt::escape(...)` (see `v0.6:src/Gui/ComposeWidget.cpp:562`). 21 sites is few enough to do the same; alternatively add one helper `UiUtils::htmlEscaped(const QString&)` and convert the sites to it — pick one approach and be consistent. |
+| `QMimeDatabase` | 4 files: `src/Composer/ComposerAttachments.cpp`, `src/Composer/MessageComposer.cpp`, `src/Gui/AttachmentView.cpp`, `src/UiUtils/PartWalker_impl.h` | No source change needed once the external QtMimeTypes library is wired up (Phase 1). Caution: the `af84b80c` revert will try to restore v0.6-era `#if`-guarded `#include "mimetypes-qt4/include/QMimeDatabase"` blocks in these files — **drop those hunks**; the plain `#include <QMimeDatabase>` resolves on both Qt versions via include paths. |
+| `QUrlQuery` | 5 files: `src/Composer/Mailto.cpp`, `src/Gui/ComposeWidget.cpp`, `src/Gui/EnvelopeView.cpp`, `src/Gui/OneEnvelopeAddress.cpp`, `src/Imap/Parser/MailAddress.cpp` | Qt4 `QUrl` has the query/encoded accessors directly. `Mailto.cpp` has the exact dual pattern in v0.6 (`encodedQueryItems()` etc.) — copy it; do the other four in the same style. |
+| `QStandardPaths` | `src/Common/Paths.cpp/.h` | Copy the v0.6 body: `QDesktopServices::storageLocation(...)` (note v0.6 maps DownloadLocation → `QDesktopServices::DocumentsLocation`). |
+| `QHeaderView::setSectionResizeMode` | 4 uses: `src/Gui/MsgListView.cpp`, `src/Gui/ShortcutHandler/ShortcutConfigWidget.cpp`, `src/Gui/Window.cpp` | Qt4 name is `setResizeMode` (enum values identical). Per-site `#if` guard, or a tiny inline helper. |
+| `QGuiApplication` / `Qt::ApplicationState` | `src/Gui/Window.cpp` (2 uses), `src/Imap/Model/Utils.cpp` | No Qt4 equivalent of `applicationStateChanged`. Guard the feature out for Qt4 (`#if QT_VERSION >= ...`) — it's a power-saving nicety, not core function. Check what `Utils.cpp` uses `QGuiApplication` for and guard similarly. |
+| `QTimer::singleShot(250, [url](){...})` | 1 use, `src/Gui/Window.cpp` | Lambda overload is Qt 5.4. Replace with a named slot + member holding the pending value, or a small single-purpose QObject. Works on both Qt versions — no guard needed. |
+
+Not problems (audited, zero uses or already Qt4-clean — don't "fix" these):
+`QRegularExpression`, `QSaveFile`, `QTimeZone`, `qCDebug`/`QLoggingCategory`,
+`Q_ENUM`, `qInfo`, `qOverload`, `QCommandLineParser`, `qEnvironmentVariableIsSet`,
+`qUtf8Printable`, `Q_DECL_OVERRIDE`, module-prefixed `<QtWidgets/...>` includes
+(there are none — bare `<QClass>` includes resolve via cmake include dirs on both).
